    {
      "title": "Iran conflict cost US more than $38 billion: Congressional Budget Office",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/world-news/iran-conflict-cost-us-more-than-38-billion-congressional-budget-office-126091600023_1.html",
      "description": "The US war against Iran has cost the Department of Defence more than USD 38 billion through Aug 1, and will continue costing up to USD 3 billion a month or more depending on the intensity of the conflict, according to an assessment released Tuesday by the nonpartisan Congressional Budget Office.\nCBO said the war is expected to contribute to inflation into the first quarter of 2027, making inflation roughly 0.5 percentage points higher than they had previously estimated. That's driven largely by the reduction of oil and natural gas shipments through the Strait of Hormuz and disruptions to shipping through the Red Sea.\nThe estimate, prepared in response to a request for information from the top Democrat on the House Budget committee, Rep Brendan Boyle, largely aligns with a previous estimate from Defence Secretary Pete Hegseth, who pinned the costs at USD 37.5 billion, according to his Senate testimony.\nThe estimates come largely from replacing munitions and equipment lost in battle,",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-09-16T03:13:11"
    },
    {
      "title": "Iran war has cost on average $246 million per day in its first five months, CBO finds",
      "link": "https://www.cnbc.com/2026/09/15/cbo-iran-war-cost-pentagon-weapons.html",
      "description": "CBO estimates the Iran war cost the Pentagon $38.1 billion through Aug. 1 and could cost another $2 billion to $3 billion each additional month.",
      "source_name": "CNBC Top News",
      "published": "2026-09-15T22:33:45"
    }
